cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this research draft, please cite the version or commit hash you consulted."
title: "Linear Nonequilibrium Information Suffices for Fault-Tolerant Subquantum Search"
type: article
authors:
  - family-names: Stay
    given-names: Michael A.
    affiliation: "Computer Science Department, University of Auckland"
    email: mike@cs.auckland.ac.nz
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-29
abstract: >-
  A conditional resource analysis of unique-witness search using nonequilibrium
  de Broglie–Bohm pointers and a syndrome-resolved error-transparent interface.
  The draft derives a linear relative-entropy nonequilibrium cost and polynomial
  fault-tolerance overhead under explicitly stated assumptions.
keywords:
  - de Broglie-Bohm theory
  - quantum nonequilibrium
  - subquantum computation
  - quantum error correction
  - fault tolerance
  - computational complexity
